ng authorization for tests and side effects. An unchecked deployment\012  or live-provider gate does not itself authorize publication or spending.\012- Do not use subagents. Use Git only inside the applicable repositories.\012\012Update the tracking file and stop this invocation:\012\012- Maintain - [ ] for incomplete gates and - [x] only for gates whose stated\012  acceptance criteria passed. Preserve IDs, unresolved criteria and dated failures.\012- Maintain compact Checked-item evidence only for acceptance gates whose current\012  state matters: ID, implemented/verified/deployed state, a short evidence reference,\012  and last relevant change. Do not accumulate one prose log entry per iteration.\012  If new evidence invalidates a checked item, reopen it with the current reason;\012  the runner-owned archive retains earlier snapshots.\012- Replace Current handoff near the top with: active checkbox, criteria closed this\012  iteration, remaining criteria, blocker/dependency, concise verification results\012  including skips, deferred gates with unblock conditions, and the exact next ready\012  checkbox. Delete superseded handoff prose rather than moving it into a history\012  section. Continue the unfinished active gate unless its documented blocker makes\012  another gate ready.\012- Keep timing and exit information concise in the current handoff: approximate\012  discovery/implementation/verification durations when useful, loaded prompt\012  revision, declared batch outcome and exit reason. Do not create a growing dated\012  iteration-history section; the runner archives each boundary snapshot separately.\012  If exiting early with an unfinished outcome, explain only the current reason.\012- Summarize concrete changes and checks; explain any scope change. If no gate\012  closed, identify the material prerequisite advanced and how it reduces the\012  remaining work. Repeated rediscovery, extra notes or adjacent tests alone\012  are not progress toward the active g